# Force LF checkout repo-wide. Rationale (clean-clone test, 2026-08-25): on Windows,
# autocrlf=true turns checkouts into CRLF, and this repo's LF-discipline tests (they guard
# "CRLF on the cluster means an incident") go red on the spot — 23 of them. A cloner seeing
# red on their very first test run is a distribution defect.
# eol=lf is a no-op on Linux/macOS and corrects checkouts on Windows; .sh/.py going to the cluster must be LF.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.svg text eol=lf
*.tgz binary
*.bundle binary
*.so binary
